{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79QZS3udq4V4ME7EYZN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the update below. It's about 400 words. It starts with the missed updates and the lost customer because investors will notice both anyway, and they'll trust you more if you raise them first. It then makes the case that the reminder results answer the competitor that just took your largest customer.\n\n- **Runway:** $480,000 at $44,000 a month is about 11 months. The draft names this as your main concern and promises a plan in the next update. If you already have a plan, such as cutting costs or a raise date, add it. Investors will look for it.\n- **Requests to investors:** You didn't give me any, so I wrote two that fit the situation. Edit or replace them if you have more specific ones.\n- **Placeholders:** Replace [Company] and [Your name] before sending.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: [Company] quarterly update: flat revenue, a big loss, and a new product launching next month\n\nHi all,\n\nFirst, an apology. You haven't heard from me in two quarters, and that was my mistake. From now on you'll get an update every quarter, whether the news is good or bad.\n\n**Headline numbers**\n- Monthly recurring revenue: $41,000, the same as three months ago\n- Clinics: 9 added, 4 lost\n- Cash: $480,000\n- Net burn: about $44,000 a month, so about 11 months of runway\n\n**The bad news**\nWe lost our largest customer this quarter, a 12-clinic chain paying $5,500 a month. They switched to the scheduler built into their electronic records system. The 9 new clinics made up for that revenue, which is why monthly revenue stayed flat instead of falling. Still, we aren't growing, and that isn't where we need to be.\n\nThis loss also taught us something. For larger groups, a basic scheduler that comes free with their records system is a real competitor. Scheduling on its own may not be enough to keep them.\n\n**The good news**\nOur automatic text reminders are working. Clinics that use them have a 7% no-show rate, compared with 13% before they started. That cuts missed appointments almost in half. Every no-show is a lost visit for the clinic, so this is the clearest value we deliver. It also works no matter which scheduler a clinic uses.\n\n**What's next**\nStarting next month, we'll sell the reminder feature on its own for $150 a month. This lets us sell to clinics that are committed to their records system's scheduler, including groups like the chain we just lost, without having to replace that scheduler. It also gives current customers another reason to stay.\n\nRunway is my main concern. In the next update I'll report how the standalone reminders are selling and what that means for our spending and fundraising plans. You'll get that update on time.\n\n**How you can help**\n1. Introductions to owners or operations leads at physical therapy clinics, especially groups with several locations that use a records system with a built-in scheduler.\n2. If you've worked with companies that sell add-on products to users of a larger platform, I'd value 20 minutes of your advice on pricing and positioning.\n\nThank you for your patience and support. I'm glad to talk with any of you one on one. Just reply to this email.\n\n[Your name]\nFounder, [Company]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5415,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5415},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19fce95b-83c9-46ad-bf51-ae80124304cc","uuid":"a63e93cc-9a10-4e14-a9a6-c052da8f4ec8","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:18:32.731Z","request_id":"req_011Ch79QZCQyE54sh9zaZeCD"}
